{
  "name": "roleALPHA: Workflows follow the organisation",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "7c3116ef-ebf3-5222-9fb1-7d6cc3e17426",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -200,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Workflows follow the organisation\nEvery 15 minutes the builder asks roleALPHA what changed since the last run (`list_changes`, one call instead of reading the whole organisation). It keeps the cursor in this workflow, so it needs no table.\n\n**Propose** decides clear cases by rule, without a model: the builder's own steps, decisions by people, steps that only group others, and steps the scheduler starts by their frequency. For the rest it asks the model, which sees all workflows and the inputs of the runner, and checks the answer. A usable proposal becomes an **inactive draft**, and every person filling the deciding role of the governing step gets an e-mail with what changes and links to approve or reject it (workflow *roleALPHA: Approve workflow drafts*). Drafts that change Code nodes go to the code governing step instead.\n\nIf the model is away the change comes back next run. What cannot be proposed at all is reported to the same people.\n\nSet the values in **Settings**, **Runner Workflow** on *Propose* and the credentials (roleALPHA MCP OAuth2, n8n API, Approval Seal, Anthropic, SMTP). The first run starts now and reports nothing from before.",
        "width": 620,
        "height": 420
      }
    },
